  "result": "I can't give you the letter for a quiz item, including on a retake, but I can tell you what q3 is probing.\n\nThe concept is **what an agent loop does when it can't make progress on its own**. The model only sees its context and decides the next action. If it is stuck in a pattern, nothing inside the loop forces it out, because the loop runs until the model stops asking for tools or the program intervenes. So the question is which option changes what the *program* does, not what the model sees or is told.\n\nThat applies to every option. For each one, ask whether it alters the loop's control flow or only the model's input. In this run, the model already has all 40 steps in view and has already been told what to do.\n\nOnce you've graded your submission, I'm happy to go through q3 with you.",
